e only child to survive infancy (Ekwefi gave birth ten times) and mirrors Ekwefi's independent strength. Ezinma and Ekwefi have a special bond, reflected in the mutual love and respect that they show one another. Ekwefi leaves her first husband and marries Okonkwo ... \",\"title\":\"https://study.com/academy/lesson/ekwefi-in-things-fall-apart.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d2\"},\"ref\":\"d2\",\"snippet\":\" ... The two developed a unique character of an innocent man-child who found himself in dramatic and hazardous circumstances with only providence and good luck making him come out on top. This character clicked with the public and Langdon enjoyed a streak of artistic and commercial successes using ... \",\"title\":\"https://m.imdb.com/search/name/?death_date=1944&ref_=nm_pdt_dth_yr\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d93\"},\"ref\":\"d93\",\"snippet\":\" ... and her child, a boy whom she names Richard. Esther and Mr Woodcourt marry and live in a Yorkshire house which Jarndyce gives to them. The couple later raise two daughters.\\n\\nMany of the novel's subplots focus on minor characters. One such subplot is the hard life ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bleak_House\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d94\"},\"ref\":\"d94\",\"snippet\":\" ... one survived,\\n\\nTwo divorced and two beheaded\\n\\nAnother popular mnemonic device is:\\n\\nDivorced, beheaded, died;\\n\\nDivorced, beheaded, survived\\n\\nThis is respectively:\\n\\nKatherine of Aragon, Anne Boleyn, Jane Seymour\\n\\nAnne of Cleves, Katherine Howard, and Katherine Parr.\\n\\nHenry VIII's six wives\\n\\nKatherine of Aragon\\n\\n1485 - 1536\